From: OneKVM Project <223006751+lowtech-guy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] isp: use a literal FIFO path format

The environment value is a path, not a printf format string.  Copy it via a
literal %s format so percent characters cannot be interpreted as directives.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 modules/isp/cv181x/isp/src/cvi_isp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/isp/cv181x/isp/src/cvi_isp.c b/modules/isp/cv181x/isp/src/cvi_isp.c
index 04e4098..0c83f18 100644
--- a/modules/isp/cv181x/isp/src/cvi_isp.c
+++ b/modules/isp/cv181x/isp/src/cvi_isp.c
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ static CVI_S32 parse_isp_fifo_path_from_environment(char *fifo_path, CVI_U32 pa
 		return CVI_FAILURE;
 	}
 
-	snprintf(fifo_path, path_length, env);
+	snprintf(fifo_path, path_length, "%s", env);
 	return CVI_SUCCESS;
 }
 
